    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This now matches the original pixel-for-pixel in layout, spacing, and typography. The clone is complete at `/var/folders/gb/m6478s0n5mx9wqlz8t_c03800000gn/T/gumshoe-agent-run-LAWplg/clone.html`.\n\nSummary:\n\n- **Source page has no CSS, nav, or design system at all.** The fetched HTML is two bare `<section>` blocks (`#hero`, `#specs`), each with an `<img>` + `<p>`, and zero `<style>`/`<link>` tags — the browser was rendering pure user-agent defaults (white background, black Arial-ish sans text, default paragraph margins). I verified this by reading the raw source directly rather than guessing at a themed design, since there was nothing themed to find.\n- **Componentization:** there's nothing to name as a reusable component — no card, button, or repeating pattern beyond the same trivial \"image + paragraph\" shape used twice. I kept the markup essentially 1:1 rather than inventing structure that isn't there.\n- **No JS-driven content** (no carousels, lazy-loading, etc.) — nothing to special-case.\n- **Images flagged as unrecreatable-as-hotlinks:** `/founder.jpg` and `/spec-icon.svg` are root-relative paths with no origin (this is a bare local file, not a live site), so there's no real absolute URL to hotlink to. I left the `src` attributes exactly as in the source, which faithfully reproduces the original's own broken-image state rather than fabricating a placeholder image.\n- **Tailwind setup:** loaded via CDN with a minimal config; used utility classes (`bg-white text-black font-sans text-base leading-[normal]`, `my-4` on paragraphs) chosen specifically to reproduce the browser's UA-stylesheet defaults, since Tailwind's Preflight reset (which forces `line-height: 1.5`) would otherwise visibly loosen the spacing versus the original's native ~1.15 line-height.\n- **Screenshot comparison:** captured `original.png` at 1280×900, then two rounds of `clone-roundN.png` at the same viewport using headless Chrome directly (no crow-nester available, so I drove Chrome's `--headless --screenshot` flags myself). Round 1 was close but had visibly taller line spacing from Tailwind's default `line-height`; round 2 fixed that with an explicit `leading-[normal]` override and now matches the original's layout, spacing, and text position essentially exactly."
    }
